  "practice": [
    "Say ও three times with a rounded o sound like the vowel in go: o, o, o.",
    "Practice ও-কার: ক + ো = কো, ত + ো = তো, ব + ো = বো, and ল + ো = লো.",
    "Notice that ো visually wraps around its consonant even though it represents one vowel sound.",
    "Use the reading shortcut ো → o in ভালো, ছোট, চোখ, and বোন."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ও is a very common Bengali vowel with a sound roughly like o in go, though its exact quality varies by accent and word.",
    "When ও is attached to a consonant, it becomes ো, called ও-কার.",
    "The ো sign visually wraps around its consonant: ক + ো = কো.",
    "Recognizing ো automatically makes a large number of everyday Bengali words easier to read."
  ]
